<p><strong>A double-booking happens when your diary lets two people claim the same therapist or room at the same time. It stops when every booking, from every channel, is checked against staff, room and time before the slot is confirmed.</strong></p>
<p><em>The scene below is a typical one, not a single named customer.</em></p>
<h2>The 6 pm Saturday problem</h2>
<p>A regular phones the front desk and is promised the 6 pm hot-stone massage. Half an hour earlier a tourist was told the same room was free, and a message on WhatsApp has also been answered with "yes, 6 pm". The register has one line, the phone has one memory and the chat has another. Three people arrive for one room.</p>
<h2>Why it keeps happening</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Many places to book.</strong> Phone, WhatsApp, Viber, walk-ins and a paper register each hold part of the truth.</li><li><strong>Only the therapist is checked.</strong> The room, or the second therapist's break, is forgotten.</li><li><strong>Several branches.</strong> A customer is promised a slot at one branch while the therapist is covering at another.</li></ul>
<h2>What it costs</h2>
<p>An awkward apology on the day, a walk-out from a customer who would have returned, and a front desk that stops trusting the diary and starts double-checking everything. Read more on <a href="/blog/stop-taking-bookings-on-whatsapp-nepal/">why WhatsApp bookings lose messages</a>.</p>
<h2>How it is solved</h2>
<p>In Zennly a booking holds the <strong>staff member, room and time together</strong>. When a slot is taken, nobody else can book it, whether they use the online page, call the desk or walk in. The same schedule is shared by every branch, so a therapist is not promised in two places. See <a href="/features/booking/">conflict-free online booking</a>.</p>
<h2>A quick fix you can start today</h2>
<ol><li>Pick one place where every booking is recorded.</li><li>Record the room as well as the therapist.</li><li>Give customers one way to book online, so they can see only free slots.</li></ol>
